Define $F(N)$ as the maximum cardinality of $A\subseteq[N]$ for which there is no ordered quadruple $(x,y,z,w)\in A^4$ with all four entries pairwise distinct and $x+3y=2z+2w$. Repetitions are excluded only by that stated distinctness requirement. Determine the growth, or a sharp asymptotic description, of $F(N)$. \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]} \href{https://arxiv.org/abs/1408.2568}{[S2]}

